# Wave W17-W (Mt. Apex — South): step flags — tiered dressed-stone flags, step-worn treads: warm mid-grey flags carrying one worn tread per flag, a soft highlight lip above a shadow tread line, the front hall’s climb written into its floor (design: two dressed-stone doors joining on paved paths that climb tiered dressed steps north). Mt. Apex — South’s own floor — split from Central’s spine flags by warmth and the treads (the hall climbs in steps, the spine runs level and cruciform) and from the shipped coronet flags of the League register by the wear: this stone is trodden by travellers, that stone is kept.
